--- Split into numbered files
data.1.tsv
data.2.tsv
data.3.tsv
data.tsv
data.1.tsv	300	300	599
data.2.tsv	300	600	899
data.3.tsv	100	900	999
data.tsv	300	0	299
1000	499500
--- The numbering continues from the number in the name of the first file
data.5.tsv
data.6.tsv
data.7.tsv
data.8.tsv
--- The number can be in the name of the first file
data.0.tsv
data.1.tsv
data.2.tsv
data.3.tsv
--- A non-numeric part of the name is not a sequence number
data.1.v2.tsv
data.2.v2.tsv
data.3.v2.tsv
data.v2.tsv
--- A new file on each insert continues the numbering as well
data.5.Parquet
data.6.Parquet
--- Without splitting everything goes into a single file
data.tsv
--- The files are truncated on the second insert with engine_file_truncate_on_insert
data.1.tsv
data.2.tsv
data.3.tsv
data.tsv
1000	499500
--- All the split files are visible for the File engine table
1000	499500	4
--- An exception if the name is already taken
FILE_ALREADY_EXISTS
--- The taken names are skipped with engine_file_allow_create_multiple_files
data.1.tsv
data.2.tsv
data.3.tsv
data.4.tsv
data.5.tsv
data.tsv
1000	499500
--- Every file is complete on its own, for a format with a prefix and a suffix
1000	499500	10
--- The size of the compressed data is taken into account
1000000	499999500000	1
